.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt GETFACL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm getfacl
.Nd display POSIX access and default ACLs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the access ACL for each
.Ar file
and, unless
.Fl d
is specified, its default ACL when one is present.
The displayed entries use the POSIX
.Dq user ,
.Dq group ,
.Dq mask
and
.Dq other
text form accepted by
.Xr setfacl 1 .
If an access ACL is not stored, the mode bits are displayed as the
equivalent three-entry ACL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr setfacl 1 ,
.Xr chmod 1
